## 12. Data Quality Governance and Responsibilities

Effective data quality management requires collaboration between business functions and technical teams.

### 12.1. Governance Roles

Executive Sponsor

Provides strategic direction, approves major resources, and resolves escalated organizational issues.

Data Management Office Director

Leads the project, coordinates stakeholders, monitors performance, and reports progress to executive management.

Data Owner

Approves data definitions, quality requirements, thresholds, and business remediation decisions.

Data Steward

Monitors data quality, investigates exceptions, coordinates corrective actions, and maintains business data definitions.

Data Quality Analyst

Develops quality measurements, conducts profiling, analyzes trends, and prepares quality reports.

IT Department

Implements technical controls, maintains integrations, and supports automated quality monitoring.

Personal Data Protection Officer / Privacy Function

Advises on personal data processing, access restrictions, and compliance requirements.

