### 13.2. Composite Data Quality Score

A weighted score can be calculated using approved business priorities.

**For this case study, the following illustrative weights are proposed:**

| Dimension | Weight |
|---|---:|
| Completeness | 20% |
| Accuracy | 25% |
| Consistency | 20% |
| Timeliness | 15% |
| Uniqueness | 10% |
| Validity | 10% |
| **Total** | **100%** |

Formula:**

Overall Data Quality Score = Σ (Dimension Score × Assigned Weight)

**Using the hypothetical final results:**

- Completeness: 99%
- Accuracy: 97%
- Consistency: 96%
- Timeliness: 95%
- Uniqueness: 98.5%
- Validity: 99%
Overall Score = (99 × 0.20) + (97 × 0.25) + (96 × 0.20) + (95 × 0.15) + (98.5 × 0.10) + (99 × 0.10)

Overall Data Quality Score = 97.25%

The composite score is an internal management indicator. It does not replace individual rule compliance, critical data quality thresholds, or applicable regulatory requirements.

