## 16. Data Protection and Compliance Considerations

The project incorporates privacy and information security requirements when processing customer data.

Because the company operates in Saudi Arabia and processes personal information, the project considers the Saudi Personal Data Protection Law (PDPL) and applicable implementing regulations.

**Key controls include:**

1. Restricting access to personal data based on authorized business responsibilities.

2. Applying data minimization principles.

3. Using de-identified or pseudonymized data for testing when feasible.

4. Maintaining audit trails for data corrections.

5. Preventing unauthorized disclosure of customer information.

6. Applying appropriate retention and disposal requirements.

7. Reviewing privacy risks associated with data matching and merging.

8. Ensuring that data quality activities have a legitimate processing purpose.

Data quality improvement must not compromise personal data protection.

The organization must also determine which SDAIA data management controls apply directly to its legal and operational context.

